  "headword": "{未解決|みかいけつ}",
  "reading": "みかいけつ",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, no-adjective",
  "gloss": "unresolved; unsolved; unsettled",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "unresolved; unsolved; unsettled",
      "explanation": "The state of something not yet being resolved or settled. Used for cases, problems, disputes, and issues that remain open. The prefix {未|み} means 'not yet.'"
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "17292_mikaiketsu_ex1",
      "japanese": "この{事件|じけん}はまだ{未解決|みかいけつ}だ。",
      "english": "This case is still unsolved.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "17292_mikaiketsu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{未解決|みかいけつ}の{問題|もんだい}がいくつか{残|のこ}っている。",
      "english": "Several unresolved problems remain.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "17292_mikaiketsu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{何十年|なんじゅうねん}も{未解決|みかいけつ}のまま{放置|ほうち}されていた{事件|じけん}に、{新|あたら}しい{手|て}がかりが{見|み}つかった。",
      "english": "A new lead was found in a case that had been left unsolved for decades.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "USAGE:\nFunctions as both a noun and a no-adjective ({未解決|みかいけつ}の{事件|じけん} 'an unsolved case'). Very common in news, law, and formal contexts. The のまま pattern ({未解決|みかいけつ}のまま 'remaining unresolved') is frequently used.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {未解決|みかいけつ}{事件|じけん} (unsolved case/cold case)\n- {未解決|みかいけつ}の{問題|もんだい} (unresolved problem)\n- {未解決|みかいけつ}のまま (remaining unresolved)\n\nRELATED {未|み}〜 WORDS:\n- {未完成|みかんせい}: unfinished, incomplete\n- {未確認|みかくにん}: unconfirmed\n- {未定|みてい}: undecided",
